[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/5771199493","html_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725#issuecomment-5771199493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725","id":5771199493,"node_id":"IC_kwDON109P88AAAABV_2EBQ","user":{"login":"SM26M","id":224298584,"node_id":"U_kgDODV6GWA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224298584?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M","html_url":"https://github.com/SM26M","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SM26M/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T04:26:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T04:26:24Z","body":"Inline spacing","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/5771199493/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/6583204155","html_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725#issuecomment-6583204155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725","id":6583204155,"node_id":"IC_kwDON109P88AAAABiGO5Ow","user":{"login":"igordev23","id":182698900,"node_id":"U_kgDOCuPDlA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182698900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23","html_url":"https://github.com/igordev23","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-02T17:04:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T17:04:12Z","body":"Independent reproduction + root-cause confirmation (found separately on 2026-10-02, before seeing this issue).\n\n**Setup:** full Compose stack with CPU-only transcription, long-lived install based on `c63ddda`, stock `vexaai/vexa-bot:v012`, `BOT_AUTHENTICATED=true`, signed-in Google profile restored from S3 (`BOT_USERDATA_S3_PATH`).\n\n**Symptom:** every authenticated Google Meet bot ended in ~10 s with `completion_reason: auth_session_missing` (3 meetings in a row, same result).\n\n**Ruling out the profile first:** the restored profile was valid. It had the Google cookies and was signed in, so this was not a login or credential problem.\n\n**Controlled experiment** (same restored profile, same args, only one variable):\n\n| Launch | Result |\n|---|---|\n| with `--incognito` (as `launchBrowser()` builds it today) | Meet renders the guest lobby → `isGoogleSignedOutLobby` → `AuthSessionError` |\n| without `--incognito` | Meet shows the signed-in account and the bot joins |\n\n**Root cause:** the same one this issue describes. `JOIN_BROWSER_ARGS` (`core/meetings/modules/join/src/browser-args.ts`) carries `--incognito`, and `launchBrowser()` (`core/meetings/services/bot/src/capture-bridge.ts`) combines it with `getAuthenticatedBrowserArgs()`. The incognito context ignores the restored `--user-data-dir`, and `remote-browser/args.ts` already notes that incognito discards cookies.\n\n**Live check of a local fix** (strip `--incognito` only when `inv.authenticated`, guest launches unchanged). I built it as a dev bot image and joined a real Meet call:\n- bot log: `Authenticated mode: skipping name input` → `✅ Bot admitted`\n- every join Chromium ran with `incognito=no` on the restored `--user-data-dir`\n- real Portuguese speech was transcribed; meeting `completed`, recording finalized\n- teardown re-synced the auth profile to storage\n\n#1873 implements the same mechanism, with a unit test on top. I'm happy to be the non-author validator for it. I have the same deployment ready and will post a multichannel attestation on the PR: a red control on stock `v012`, green on the PR head, and a guest-launch regression check.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/6583204155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/6685284740","html_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725#issuecomment-6685284740","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725","id":6685284740,"node_id":"IC_kwDON109P88AAAABjnlZhA","user":{"login":"koraykupe","id":5278340,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzgzNDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5278340?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe","html_url":"https://github.com/koraykupe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/koraykupe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-06T12:54:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T12:54:17Z","body":"Confirming this on a self-hosted single-machine install, `v0.12.28` (compose, `BOT_AUTHENTICATED=true`, S3 userdata on versitygw).\n\nEvery authenticated Google Meet join failed with `auth_session_missing` / \"Browser profile signed out\", even a few minutes after a fresh `provision-cli` login. The bot screenshot showed the guest lobby (\"What's your name?\").\n\nWhat isolated it:\n- Restoring the same `userdata` profile into a fresh `vexa-bot:v0.12.28` container and launching with `getAuthenticatedBrowserArgs()` only: `myaccount.google.com` and `meet.google.com/home` are both signed in.\n- Same run with `--incognito` appended: redirected to `google.com/account/about` and the Meet marketing page, i.e. signed out. (Side note: `validateLoggedIn` still returned `loggedIn: true` in that case, because the auth cookies are visible via `context.cookies()` even though the incognito page doesn't use them.)\n- Rebuilding the bot image with `\"--incognito\",` removed from `modules/join/dist/browser-args.js`: the bot joined as the signed-in account and went `active` with no waiting room.\n\nSo the approach in #1873 matches what fixed it for us. One more thing showed up right after this fix, filed separately: the signed-in lobby CTA can read \"Join anyway\", which isn't in `googleAuthJoinCtaSelectors`.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/6685284740/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]